course: dictionary
lesson: 2698
title: Shy and unsure
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words describe how a person feels inside, and the clues around them show what they do. Read this from the summer play: «the diffident and delaying dog-rose». The flower is slow to come on stage, so it is holding back. Diffident means shy and not sure of yourself.
explain: Clues help you spot diffident. A diffident child might know the answer but not put a hand up. Ask yourself: is this person holding back, staying quiet, or waiting to be asked? If yes, diffident probably means shy.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «The shy and delaying dog-rose» still makes sense, so shy is the right meaning. Diffident is not the same as rude or angry. It is about being quiet and unsure.
fact: Diffident means shy and not sure of yourself.
fact: Diffident also means not wanting to speak up or push yourself forward.
fact: In the summer play, «the diffident and delaying dog-rose» is a flower that holds back before it appears.
fact: Diffident is an adjective: diffident, more diffident, most diffident.
fact: Mole is diffident at first with the grand Badger, so he does not rush to speak.
exercise: In the play, «the diffident and delaying dog-rose» is slow to come on. What does diffident mean? | Very angry | Tall and green | *Shy and not sure of yourself | Loud and bold
exercise: Mole is diffident at first with the grand Badger. Which word means the same as diffident? | *Shy | Bold | Cheerful | Hungry
exercise: A child knows the answer but does not put a hand up. Which word describes her? | Treacherous | Luminous | Famished | *Diffident
test: «Purple loosestrife arrived early», then «the diffident and delaying dog-rose» came on. Why might the dog-rose wait before showing itself? | It is giving out light | *It is shy and not sure of itself | It is shouting for attention | It is very hungry
test: Which sentence shows a diffident person? | He shouted across the playground for his friends | He told a loud joke to the whole class | *He stood at the back and let the others go first | He waved his hand at once to answer first
exam: Which word best fits a person who is quiet, modest and unsure about pushing themselves forward? | Ancient | Luminous | Curt | *Diffident
